>
  <p class="lead-para">
    <strong>PCB career options fall into eight lanes, and MBBS is only one of them.</strong>
    The others are nursing and allied health, pharma and clinical research, psychology and nutrition, life-science research, agriculture and food, health-tech and data, and a set of non-science pivots.
    Pick the lane that fits your energy, your family budget and the skills you can prove, and you build a high-value skill portfolio that can open higher income options and earlier financial freedom. Pick by label and you risk years and lakhs on the wrong one.
  </p>

  <div class="key-takeaways">
    <p class="key-takeaways__label">The short version</p>
    <ul>
      <li>In 2026 close to 20 lakh students appeared for NEET UG and about 11.21 lakh qualified, against roughly 1.41 lakh MBBS seats. For most PCB students the real plan is a lane, not one exam.</li>
      <li>Shortlist two lanes with the 4-Checkpoint Protocol (your own biology, context, market and survival), then check the official entry gate for each before paying for coaching or admission.</li>
      <li><strong>Your next practical step: build one small piece of proof in each shortlisted lane, such as a note, a literature summary or a tiny data sheet. Skill plus proof lifts income in every lane.</strong></li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <p>
    Every direction PCB opens, with the entry rule and the money reality for each, is mapped below. More detail on single questions sits in our <a href="/blog/career-options/">career options guides</a>.
    If you want a person to test your shortlist against your marks, budget and family situation, <a href="https://futurecareerschool.com/services/career-counselling-and-career-guidance/">continuous career guidance</a> builds a high-value skill portfolio around your shortlist, and the <a href="/career-skills-compass/">Career &amp; Skills Compass</a> is a quick first read on your strengths.
  </p>

  <p>
    Whether your board calls it PCB, BiPC or Intermediate, the base is the same: Physics, Chemistry and Biology. Everything here applies to all of you.
  </p>

  <div class="situation-grid">
    {situationCards.map((item) => (
