  <h2 id="not-a-career">PCB is a starting key, not a career</h2>

  <p>
    Students ask questions like "what if NEET does not work out?", "is there anything besides MBBS?" and "which field has good scope and pay without NEET?". Titles like these fill student Q&amp;A boards such as Careers360, and they all come from one hidden assumption: that PCB points at a single door.
  </p>

  <p>
    It does not. PCB is a subject combination that qualifies you for some gates and does not qualify you for others. Knowing both lists is the first useful step.
  </p>

  <div class="comparison-grid">
    <div class="compare-card compare-card--teal">
      <div class="compare-card__label">What PCB unlocks</div>
      <ul>
        {unlocks.map((item) => <li>{item}</li>)}
      </ul>
    </div>
    <div class="compare-card compare-card--gold">
      <div class="compare-card__label">What PCB alone does not unlock</div>
      <ul>
        {closes.map((item) => <li>{item}</li>)}
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="callout callout--amber">
    <p class="callout__eyebrow">Three ideas to drop early</p>
    <ul class="callout__list">
      <li>"PCB means doctor or disappointment." False and damaging. Medicine is one lane, and a respected title is not the same as the right daily work.</li>
      <li>"No NEET means no health career." Partly true. Andhra Pradesh already asks nursing applicants to appear in NEET, and BPT and BOT are due to follow nationally from 2027-28. See the section on why the no-NEET map keeps shifting.</li>
      <li>"Biology students cannot work in technology." Health-tech and bioinformatics reward exactly your domain knowledge, provided you build a quantitative floor.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <h2 id="neet-maths">The NEET seat and rank maths</h2>

  <p>
    Look at the numbers once, calmly, because they explain why planning only around one exam is risky.
  </p>

  <div class="stat-grid">
    {arithmeticStats.map((item) => (
      <div class="stat-card">
        <div class="stat-card__num">{item.num}</div>
        <p>{item.label}</p>
      </div>
    ))}
  </div>

  <p>
    Divide the two big figures and you get roughly one MBBS seat for every 14 candidates who sat the paper. Among the 11.21 lakh who qualified, that is about eight qualified candidates for each MBBS seat. Qualifying also feeds BDS, AYUSH, veterinary and, in some states, nursing counselling, so the pressure is wider than the MBBS count shows.
  </p>

  <p>
    The government seats are the ones families can afford, and there are fewer of them. Only 64,121 of the 1,40,664 MBBS seats are government seats, so about 17 qualifiers compete for each one. Private seats are 54 percent of the matrix, and that is where fees decide who joins.
  </p>

  <div class="table-wrap">
    <table class="paths-table">
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th>Stage</th>
          <th>Numbers</th>
          <th>The sum</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        {funnelRows.map((row) => (
          <tr>
            <td data-label="Stage"><strong>{row.stage}</strong></td>
            <td data-label="Numbers">{row.numbers}</td>
            <td data-label="The sum">{row.sum}</td>
          </tr>
        ))}
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <p class="note-line">
    Seat counts are from NMC's revised matrix as reported on 21 September 2026 and change with counselling. NEET PG figures are a coaching-site tally that includes DNB seats and repeat candidates, so read them as a rough scale, not an exact ratio.
  </p>

  <p>
    For students in Andhra Pradesh and Telangana, the revised matrix lists 7,615 and 10,500 MBBS seats respectively (AP: 3,565 government and 4,050 private; Telangana: 4,400 government and 6,100 private), excluding national institutes such as AIIMS and JIPMER.
  </p>

  <div class="honest-take">
    <p class="honest-take__label">Honest take</p>
    <p>
      Competition in medicine comes at two separate stages. NEET UG decides who gets into MBBS or BDS. A separate, harder NEET PG decides who gets a specialist seat years later, and specialist status is what usually drives income. A path can clear the first filter and still face the second.
    </p>
    <p>
      The legal minimum is lighter than the social expectation. After MBBS, a compulsory rotating internship of at least twelve months and registration are what permit independent practice; a postgraduate degree is not legally required to practise as a doctor. It is what most people need to reach specialist-level income, so count the runway honestly: about five and a half years for MBBS with internship, then about three more for MD or MS, before any clinic setup or years of building patient trust.
    </p>
    <p>
      The seat matrix is tentative and counselling rounds add seats, so check the current notice on the MCC site for your round.
    </p>
  </div>

  <h2 id="eight-lanes">PCB career options, sorted into eight lanes</h2>

  <p>
    These lanes are ordered by realistic growth headroom, meaning how far income and independence can stretch with skill and proof, not by prestige or exam difficulty. That is a judgement, not a rule. Lane 1 leads because the skill travels across employers and can be sold remotely. Medicine sits third because its ceiling is very high but reaching it needs two competitive stages and a long runway.
  </p>

  <div class="lane-grid">
    {lanes.map((lane) => (
      <div class:list={['lane-card', `lane-card--${lane.tone}`]}>
        <span class="lane-card__badge">{lane.badge}</span>
        <div class="lane-card__title">{lane.title}</div>
        <p class="lane-card__entry"><strong>How you enter:</strong> {lane.entry}</p>
        <p>{lane.take}</p>
        <div class="lane-row lane-row--fit"><span>Best for</span> {lane.best}</div>
        <div class="lane-row lane-row--watch"><span>Watch out</span> {lane.watch}</div>
        <p class="lane-card__read">
          Read next: <a href={lane.read.href}>{lane.read.label}</a>
          {lane.read2 && (<>{' '}or <a href={lane.read2.href}>{lane.read2.label}</a></>)}
        </p>
      </div>
    ))}
  </div>

  <div class="highlight-box highlight-box--teal">
    <p>
      <strong>Scalable ownership inside these lanes:</strong> an owned pharmacy, an independent physiotherapy or dental clinic, a nutrition or counselling practice, and a consulting or freelance health-data service all give you pricing control, the ability to hire and repeat local income that a fixed salary never offers. Each needs registration, credibility and a patient or client base, so treat it as a later stage, not a first-year plan.
    </p>
  </div>

  <h2 id="entry-gates">Entry gates, checked against official notices</h2>

  <p>
    Save this table. Entry rules change every cycle, so the last column says exactly what to verify on the official page.
  </p>

  <div class="table-wrap">
    <table class="paths-table">
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th>Route</th>
          <th>Entry gate</th>
          <th>What to check</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
