    </table>
  </div>

  <p class="note-line">
    Sources: NTA and NMC data for NEET, the Dr NTR University of Health Sciences notification for Andhra Pradesh nursing, NCAHP's March 2026 letter on BPT and BOT, the NTA CUET page for ICAR, and IISER for IAT. Always confirm on the official portal before you decide.
  </p>

  <h2 id="neet-shift">Why "without NEET" keeps shifting</h2>

  <p>
    Many guides, videos and forum answers still say nursing and physiotherapy need no NEET. That was mostly true, and it is now true only in parts.
  </p>

  <p>
    Andhra Pradesh moved its four-year BSc Nursing admission to NEET UG from 2026-27 for government and private colleges, in place of the earlier state test. The NTR University of Health Sciences notification asks applicants to have appeared in NEET UG 2026 and to hold 45 percent in science subjects (40 percent for SC, ST and BC).
  </p>

  <p>
    Physiotherapy and occupational therapy took a different turn. The National Commission for Allied and Healthcare Professions first asked for NEET from 2026-27, and Karnataka's allied council even directed universities to admit through NEET scores in January 2026. In March 2026 the commission wrote to UGC that NEET is not mandatory for BPT and BOT in 2026-27 and deferred it to 2027-28, citing the logistics of adding two more courses to an exam already under way.
  </p>

  <p>
    So the honest answer for a student finishing Class 12 in 2027 is to plan on NEET for BPT and BOT, and to confirm it against the notice for your state. Two rule changes inside one year is the reason old answers on forums go stale.
  </p>

  <div class="callout callout--amber">
    <p class="callout__eyebrow">What this means for you</p>
    <ul class="callout__list">
      <li>Sit NEET even if MBBS is not your goal. Appearing keeps AYUSH, veterinary, nursing in states like Andhra Pradesh and, from 2027-28, physiotherapy and occupational therapy counselling open.</li>
      <li>Ask each college which route applies to your state and year. Do not rely on last year's answer.</li>
      <li>Colleges that promise admission "without any exam" for regulated courses deserve extra checking of their approvals.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <p>
    The NCAHP Act 2021 itself groups allied and healthcare work into ten categories, including medical laboratory and life sciences, physiotherapy, nutrition science, ophthalmic sciences, occupational therapy, medical radiology and imaging, and health information management. That breadth is why allied health is a real career lane and not a consolation prize.
  </p>

  <h2 id="weekly-reality">What a working week looks like</h2>

  <p>
    A respected title is not the same as the right daily work. Compare the boring 80 percent before you compare pay.
  </p>

  <div class="week-grid">
